  "title": "Hurrian Hymn to Nikkal",
  "summary": "A clay tablet from the Royal Palace at Ugarit (Ras Shamra, in Syria) carries the Hurrian Hymn to Nikkal, a prayer to the goddess Nikkal written in Hurrian in cuneiform with tuning instructions for a lyre. Dated between 1400 and 1200 BCE and found in the early 1950s, it is described as the world's oldest known musical notation.",
